{"what_happened": "During a scheduled CM shift (G2), coordinator U0158 read P00773's record once for 69s on CM workstation D0182 (L1, G1, G6). P00773 had no encounter in the period and no recorded link to U0158 (G3, G4).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "The read occurred inside U0158's scheduled 07:00-15:00 CM shift.", "sources": ["L1", "G2"]},
  {"claim": "U0158 is a full-time CM coordinator using a CM workstation, consistent with departmental work.", "sources": ["G1", "G6", "L1"]},
  {"claim": "The same day U0158 accessed many other patients across several units, consistent with an active coordination workload, though no fact ties P00773 to it.", "sources": ["L2", "L31"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "P00773 has no encounter in the period, so no documented clinical context explains the read.", "sources": ["G3"]},
  {"claim": "The identity graph shows no connection between U0158 and P00773, leaving the access with no shown work or personal basis.", "sources": ["G4"]},
  {"claim": "The P00773 access is a single early read, separate from the day's later multi-patient activity.", "sources": ["L1", "L2"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Whether P00773 was on U0158's care-coordination panel or the subject of a referral or task (G1-G4 show none).",
  "Whether P00773 had an encounter outside the reviewed period or under another service (G3 covers only the period).",
  "U0158's or the supervisor's stated reason for opening the record."
 ],
 "disposition": "verify",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "The read happened on shift, from the user's own CM device, with no personal link to the patient. But no fact shows a job-related purpose, and P00773's lack of any encounter leaves the access unexplained. No standalone concern appears, so it should be verified with the supervisor rather than cleared or escalated."
}

{"what_happened": "On 2026-10-04, U0170 (ICU nurse scheduled in ED that day, G1-G2) accessed P03208 21 times between 11:48 and 12:38 from ED workstations, during the patient's ED emergency encounter (G4), performing reads plus create/update actions (G29).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "The access window (11:48:11-12:38:47) falls within P03208's ED emergency encounter (11:37:50-12:37:50); the final entry is about one minute after encounter close", "sources": ["L1", "L21", "G4"]},
  {"claim": "U0170 was scheduled 07:00-15:00 in ED on the access date, covering the entire access window", "sources": ["G2", "L1"]},
  {"claim": "All five devices used during the access are ED workstations", "sources": ["L1", "L3", "L5", "L7", "L18", "G11", "G15", "G19", "G23", "G28"]},
  {"claim": "Actions combine read, update, and create categories per the action taxonomy", "sources": ["L4", "L10", "L15", "G29"]},
  {"claim": "The identity graph holds no connection between U0170 and P03208", "sources": ["G8"]},
  {"claim": "At least eight other users accessed P03208 the same day across ED, PHARM, LAB, and PCP devices", "sources": ["L46", "L60", "L61", "L69", "G12", "G13", "G21", "G25"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "U0170's home unit is ICU while the encounter and devices are ED; the day's ED schedule accounts for this mismatch", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "G4"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Optional: confirmation that the ED schedule (G2) reflects an actual ED assignment (e.g., float/coverage) rather than a scheduling error",
  "Optional: confirmation that the create/update entries (e.g., L10, L15) correspond to nursing documentation in the chart"
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Access occurred inside the patient's active ED emergency encounter (G4) by a user scheduled in ED that shift (G2), from ED workstations (G11, G15, G19, G23, G28), with read/update/create actions (G29) and no personal connection (G8). The ICU home unit (G1) is explained by the ED schedule. Nothing calls for review."
}

{"what_happened": "On 2026-10-27 at 11:39, billing coder U0265 ran one query and two reads on patient P01940 from a BILL workstation during their scheduled shift, between similar accesses to many other patients that day.",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "U0265 is a full-time coder in Billing and was scheduled there 08:00-17:00 on 2026-10-27, so the 11:39 access fell inside the scheduled BILL shift.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "L1"]},
  {"claim": "The access ran on D0390, a BILL workstation, and every device U0265 used that day (D0256, D0129, D0390) is a BILL device.", "sources": ["L1", "G12", "G10", "G11", "L4", "L26"]},
  {"claim": "The actions on P01940 (A0374 query; A0165 and A0335 reads) are the same read/query mix U0265 applied across dozens of other patient accesses the same day, with no print, copy, or update on this patient.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G13", "L4", "L15", "L30", "L33"]},
  {"claim": "P01940 had five encounters in the two weeks before the access (ORTH 10-15 and 10-21, ED 10-21 and 10-22, PCP 10-23), so the chart was recently active.", "sources": ["G3", "G4", "G5", "G6", "G7"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "No fact documents that P01940 was assigned to U0265 or that a billing task required this record; the identity graph shows no connection between user and patient, so any purpose rests on context alone.", "sources": ["G8"]},
  {"claim": "The access was read/query only, lasting about 51 seconds, with no print, copy, or update on P01940, limiting exposure if the purpose is not confirmed.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G13"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Whether P01940 was on U0265's assigned coding worklist for 2026-10-27 (BILL supervisor confirmation).",
  "Whether U0265's daily patient volume and action mix match their normal coding productivity.",
  "Whether hospital policy requires a documented record assignment before a coder opens a chart."
 ],
 "disposition": "verify",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Coder accessed the record on a BILL device during their scheduled shift amid a day-long queue of similar accesses, and the graph shows no personal tie to the patient. These facts neither establish a job purpose for this record nor show a concern, so the supervisor should confirm the record was assigned for coding before clearing."
}

{"what_happened": "During a scheduled CM shift, coordinator U0200 ran a query (A0048, 47s) and a read (A0335, 100s) on patient P03375 at 14:07-14:10 from CM workstation D0105 (L1, L2; G1, G2, G16, G30). Earlier that day P03375 was seen in the ED for drug overdose (G4).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "U0200 is a full-time CM coordinator scheduled in CM 07:00-15:00 on 2026-10-10; the reviewed access at 14:07-14:08 fell within that shift.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "L1", "L2"]},
  {"claim": "Both actions ran on D0105, a workstation in CM, the user's own department.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "G16", "G1"]},
  {"claim": "P03375 had an ED encounter the same day (07:49-09:49, reason drug overdose), so the record concerned active care that day; no fact shows CM involvement in that encounter.", "sources": ["G4"]},
  {"claim": "U0200 accessed many other patients' records across the same shift, a pattern consistent with routine workload rather than a single targeted chart.", "sources": ["L3-L32"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "The identity graph shows no connection between U0200 and P03375, and no fact documents a care-management assignment, so a job-related purpose is not evidenced.", "sources": ["G8"]},
  {"claim": "The record's same-day encounter carries reason 'Drug overdose'; the facts show no link between U0200 and that episode.", "sources": ["G4"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Whether P03375 was on U0200's CM workload on 2026-10-10 (assignment, worklist, or referral tied to the same-day ED visit) - no fact shows this (G8, G4).",
  "Whether the other patients U0200 reviewed that shift (L3-L32) were CM-assigned, which would confirm a routine-worklist pattern.",
  "Whether the 47s query and 100s read match a standard CM lookup for this patient (L1, L2, G30)."
 ],
 "disposition": "verify",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Access occurred on shift, from a CM workstation (G1, G2, G16), and no personal tie exists (G8), so no concern stands on its own. Yet no fact shows P03375 was on U0200's CM workload, so purpose is unconfirmed. Ask the supervisor to verify assignment; low priority given the routine pattern (L3-L32)."
}

{"what_happened": "On 2026-09-30 at 16:25, PCP clerk U0034 made two entries in P01882's record — an update (A0264) and a create (A0282) — from PCP workstation D0202 (L1, L2, G14, G18), during the patient's active PCP encounter E000121 (G5) and within U0034's scheduled shift (G2).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "U0034 is a full-time clerk in PCP, scheduled 08:00-17:00 that day; both accesses (16:25) fall inside the shift.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "L1", "L2"]},
  {"claim": "P01882 had an active PCP clinic encounter, E000121 (16:16:19-16:31:19), containing both access timestamps.", "sources": ["G5", "L1", "L2"]},
  {"claim": "A department-of-encounter connection links U0034's department (PCP) to encounter E000121 for P01882.", "sources": ["G9", "G1"]},
  {"claim": "Both accesses were made from D0202, a workstation in PCP, the user's own department.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "G14", "G1"]},
  {"claim": "The same afternoon U0034 accessed many other patients (e.g., L3, L15, L30, L32), and several other users accessed P01882 from PCP devices (e.g., L33, L43, L50; G12, G10, G17), showing broad same-day activity rather than sole focus on this record.", "sources": ["L3", "L15", "L30", "L32", "L33", "L43", "L50", "G12", "G10", "G17"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "A 'proximity' connection links U0034 to P01882; no fact explains its nature, so a personal link cannot be excluded from the record alone.", "sources": ["G8"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "What the 'proximity' connection (G8) represents (e.g., address proximity versus a personal relationship).",
  "What the update (A0264) and create (A0282) actually changed or added in P01882's record.",
  "Whether the care team expected a clerk's update/create during encounter E000121."
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "U0034, a PCP clerk on shift (G1, G2), accessed P01882 during the patient's active PCP encounter E000121 (G5) from a PCP workstation (G14), with a documented department-encounter link (G9). The unexplained 'proximity' flag (G8) is noted but does not outweigh the shown job-related purpose. Clear; confirm the proximity link's meaning as follow-up."
}

{"what_happened": "On 2026-10-14, LAB technician U0186 read P00287 (L1) then made a create entry, A0282 (L2, G19), from shared LAB workstation D0219 (G13) at ~10:00, inside their scheduled LAB shift (G2) and ~21 minutes after the patient's ED encounter ended (G5).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
   {"claim": "U0186 is a full-time LAB technician scheduled in LAB 07:00-15:00 on 2026-10-14; the reviewed access at 09:59:59 and 10:00:24 fell within that shift.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "L1", "L2"]},
   {"claim": "An order was sent to department LAB tying U0186 to encounter E000179, P00287's emergency visit earlier that same day, giving a direct job-related link to this patient.", "sources": ["G6", "G5"]},
   {"claim": "The access used D0219, a shared workstation in LAB, matching the user's department and scheduled work location.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "G13", "G2"]},
   {"claim": "P00287 was an active patient that morning: an ED encounter ran 08:38:56-09:38:56, and multiple other users (U0002, U0033, U0203) accessed the record around the same time, including from ED workstations.", "sources": ["G5", "L30", "L32", "L38", "L57", "L59"]},
   {"claim": "The read-then-create sequence (A0005 then A0282, a create per G19) is consistent with reviewing and resulting the LAB order rather than browsing.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "G19", "G6"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
   {"claim": "None stands on its own: the ~21-minute gap after the ED encounter ended is accounted for by the order sent to LAB (G6), and no fact shows a personal connection between U0186 and P00287.", "sources": ["G5", "G6", "L1"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
   "Whether U0186 was the assigned technologist on the LAB order for E000179 (G6 links user, department, and encounter but does not state an assignment role).",
   "What the A0282 create wrote (G19 labels it only 'create'); confirm it was the result or order entry for E000179.",
   "Whether any personal relationship exists between U0186 and P00287; no fact addresses this, so none is assumed."
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "U0186, a scheduled LAB technician (G1, G2), accessed P00287 from a LAB workstation (G13) ~21 minutes after the patient's ED encounter (G5), with an order sent to LAB for that encounter (G6); many users accessed this active patient that morning (L30-L59). Facts show a job-related purpose; no personal connection appears. Clear, low priority."
}

{"what_happened": "Nurse U0359 accessed inpatient P00311's record 27 times between 16:05 and 21:21 on 2026-10-25 (L1-L27), entirely within their scheduled SURG evening shift (G2), from SURG workstations D0357 and D0072 (G15, G9), performing a mix of reads, creates, and updates (G17).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
   {"claim": "U0359 is a SURG nurse scheduled 15:00-23:00 on 2026-10-25, and every reviewed access (16:05:21-21:21:50) falls inside that shift.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "L1", "L27"]},
   {"claim": "P00311 was an inpatient in SURG from 2026-10-20T20:48 to 2026-10-27T20:48, so the access date falls within an active stay in U0359's own unit.", "sources": ["G7"]},
   {"claim": "The identity graph links U0359's department (SURG) to encounter E002708 of P00311.", "sources": ["G8"]},
   {"claim": "All accesses came from D0357 and D0072, both workstations in SURG.", "sources": ["L1", "L16", "G15", "G9"]},
   {"claim": "Actions mix reads with creates and updates (e.g., A0282 create at L2, A0264 update at L1, A0335 read at L8); no print (A0159/A0270) or copy (A0386) action appears on P00311 in L1-L27.", "sources": ["G17", "L1", "L2", "L8"]},
   {"claim": "Other staff also accessed P00311 the same day, including from SURG workstations (e.g., U0386 on D0232/D0285/D0355), consistent with an actively treated unit patient.", "sources": ["L59", "L74", "L76", "G10", "G11", "G14"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
   {"claim": "The active SURG encounter's reason is a sensitive diagnosis (dependent drug abuse); however, the only user-patient link any fact shows is departmental (G8), and no fact shows a personal connection, so this does not stand as a concern on its own.", "sources": ["G7", "G8"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
   "Which encounter(s) of P00311 the accesses targeted: the logs do not tie lines to encounter IDs, and the patient also has ORTH, ICU, and CARD encounters that week (G3-G6).",
   "Whether U0359 was individually assigned to P00311's care team; G8 shows only a department-level link, not a personal assignment."
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "Scheduled SURG nurse (G1, G2) accessed during shift from SURG workstations (G9, G15) a patient with an active SURG inpatient stay (G7); the graph links the user's department to that encounter (G8). Actions mix reads, creates, updates with no print/copy on this patient (G17, L1-L27). No personal connection or off-shift access is shown. Clear, low."
}

{"what_happened": "During her scheduled CARD shift [G1, G2], nurse U0049 made three accesses to patient P00273 (two A0048 queries, one A0335 read) from CARD workstation D0024 [L1, L2, L3, G7, G11]. P00273 is a CARD staff member and U0049's department co-worker [G5, G6]; the only documented encounters are ED visits for migraine on 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-12 [G3, G4].",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "The access fell within U0049's scheduled 08:00-17:00 CARD shift and was made from a CARD workstation", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "G7", "L1", "L2", "L3"]},
  {"claim": "U0049 was actively working other patients on CARD devices immediately before and after this access, consistent with an active work session", "sources": ["L4", "L15", "L23", "L29", "L33"]},
  {"claim": "No fact shows a job-related purpose for this patient: P00273's only documented encounters are ED visits for migraine, and no CARD encounter or care role for U0049 is shown", "sources": ["G3", "G4", "G1"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "P00273 is a staff member in CARD and a department co-worker of U0049, a personal connection", "sources": ["G5", "G6"]},
  {"claim": "The access occurred 15 days after P00273's most recent documented encounter (an ED visit), with no treatment relationship between U0049 and P00273 shown", "sources": ["G4", "L1"]},
  {"claim": "Access was limited to queries and reads; no update, print, or create actions on this patient, which bounds exposure", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G11"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Whether P00273 has any CARD clinic encounter, referral, or upcoming appointment that would give U0049 a treatment-related reason to open the record",
  "Whether U0049 had an approved work reason (e.g., employee-health or pre-visit preparation) to access a co-worker's record",
  "U0049's or the supervisor's explanation for the access, and whether policy requires documented justification for staff-patient record access"
 ],
 "disposition": "escalate",
 "priority": "medium",
 "rationale": "Facts show a personal connection - the patient is U0049's CARD co-worker and a staff member [G5, G6] - and no job-related purpose: only ED migraine encounters weeks earlier, no CARD care shown [G3, G4]. Read-only, in-shift access bounds severity [L1, L2, L3, G2, G11]. Personal connection without shown purpose: escalate; medium."}

{"what_happened": "During a scheduled CM shift (G2), coordinator U0370 ran a 37-second query (A0048) on inpatient P03084 from a shared MED2 workstation (L1, G12, G18); the identity graph also flags a 'proximity' connection between them (G5).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "U0370 is a full-time CM coordinator with a usual evening shift (G1) and was scheduled in CM 15:00-23:00 on 2026-10-20, covering the 18:41 access (G2).", "sources": ["G1", "G2"]},
  {"claim": "The access came from D0144, a shared workstation in MED2 (G12), where P03084 was an active inpatient 2026-10-15 to 2026-10-24 (G4); another user accessed the same patient from D0144 nine minutes later (L42).", "sources": ["G4", "G12", "L42"]},
  {"claim": "U0370 accessed many other patients across the same shift on multiple devices, so the reviewed access sits inside a broad working session rather than an isolated lookup.", "sources": ["L2", "L15", "L18", "L24", "L31"]},
  {"claim": "Multiple other users accessed P03084 the same day across MED2, LAB, and RAD devices, consistent with active inpatient care; this is context only and does not show U0370's own purpose.", "sources": ["L32", "L40", "L53", "L61"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "The identity graph flags a 'proximity' connection between U0370 and P03084 (G5); no fact defines this connection or shows a job-related basis for it.", "sources": ["G5"]},
  {"claim": "No provided fact ties U0370 to P03084's care, and the patient's encounters carry a behavioral-health diagnosis, raising sensitivity if the purpose is personal.", "sources": ["G3", "G4"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "What the 'proximity' connection (G5) represents - e.g., whether it reflects a personal relationship between U0370 and P03084.",
  "Whether U0370's CM role includes P03084's case; no fact shows a care or case-management assignment.",
  "Whether U0370 had a CM duty in MED2 that evening explaining work from D0144 (G12) rather than the CM area (G8)."
 ],
 "disposition": "verify",
 "priority": "medium",
 "rationale": "On-shift CM coordinator (G1, G2) queried the record from a MED2 workstation where the patient was admitted (G4, G12), within a busy multi-patient session (L2-L31). But no fact shows a care assignment, and the unexplained proximity link (G5) on a sensitive-diagnosis patient (G3, G4) leaves purpose unproven - ask the supervisor."
}

{"what_happened": "Nurse U0157 accessed inpatient P01979's record five times on 2026-10-12 between 12:07 and 12:51 (L1-L5), performing reads plus create/update actions (G21) from two MED1 workstations (G15, G19) during a shift the user was scheduled to work in MED1 (G2).",
 "purpose_evidence": [
  {"claim": "U0157 was scheduled in MED1 on 2026-10-12 from 07:00 to 15:00, and all five accesses fall inside that window.", "sources": ["G2", "L1", "L5"]},
  {"claim": "P01979 was a MED1 inpatient from 2026-10-09 to 2026-10-14, so the patient was on the unit where U0157 was scheduled at the time of the accesses.", "sources": ["G3", "G2"]},
  {"claim": "All reviewed accesses came from MED1 workstations D0265 and D0365.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L4", "L5", "G15", "G19"]},
  {"claim": "The actions mix reads (A0335) with create (A0082, A0282) and update (A0264), a pattern consistent with clinical documentation rather than viewing alone.", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L5", "G21"]},
  {"claim": "In the same hours U0157 accessed at least four other patients (P01642, P01990, P00309, P00010), also from MED1 devices, indicating a unit-wide workload rather than a single-patient focus.", "sources": ["L6", "L8", "L12", "L34", "G11", "G16", "G8", "G18"]},
  {"claim": "Other staff (U0254, U0081, U0206, U0200) also accessed P01979 the same day from MED1 devices, consistent with team care of an active inpatient.", "sources": ["L36", "L44", "L52", "L60", "G13", "G20", "G15"]}
 ],
 "risk_indicators": [
  {"claim": "None identified: the identity graph records no connection between U0157 and P01979 (G6), all accesses fall within the scheduled shift (G2), and the patient's same-day ED encounter (20:55-21:55) postdates the reviewed accesses, so it does not explain or taint them.", "sources": ["G6", "G2", "G4", "L1", "L5"]}
 ],
 "missing_information": [
  "Whether U0157 was specifically assigned to P01979's care; the facts show unit-level alignment (schedule plus admission), not a named assignment (G2, G3).",
  "Confirmation that the 2026-10-12 MED1 schedule entry reflects a worked float assignment, since U0157's home unit is SURG (G1, G2)."
 ],
 "disposition": "clear",
 "priority": "low",
 "rationale": "U0157 was scheduled in MED1 (G2) while P01979 was a MED1 inpatient (G3); all five accesses came from MED1 workstations (G15, G19) within shift hours, mixing reads with create/update (G21), amid a multi-patient workload (L6-L35) and team-wide access (L36-L65). No personal connection is recorded (G6). Job-related pattern; clear, low priority."
}

{"what_happened": "Nurse U0098 accessed inpatient P01661's record 13 times between 00:16 and 05:09 on 2026-10-11 (L1-L13), using read, update, create, query, print, and copy actions (G24), all from MED2 workstations during a scheduled MED2 night shift (G2, G15, G16).",
"purpose_evidence": [
{"claim": "U0098 is a full-time night-shift ICU nurse (G1) and was scheduled in MED2 from 2026-10-10T23:00 to 2026-10-11T07:00, a window covering every reviewed access.", "sources": ["G1", "G2", "L1", "L13"]},
{"claim": "P01661 was an inpatient in MED2 from 2026-10-08 to 2026-10-14, so the patient was on the unit where U0098 was scheduled at the time of the accesses.", "sources": ["G6", "L1-L13"]},
{"claim": "All reviewed accesses came from MED2 workstations D0103 and D0115.", "sources": ["L1-L13", "G15", "G16"]},
{"claim": "During the same shift U0098 accessed multiple other patients, all shown from MED2 workstations, consistent with unit-wide care duties.", "sources": ["L14-L43", "G11", "G14", "G17", "G18", "G20", "G21", "G22", "G23"]},
{"claim": "The identity graph holds no connection between U0098 and P01661, so no personal relationship is indicated.", "sources": ["G9"]},
{"claim": "Other staff also accessed P01661 the same day, consistent with an active inpatient stay.", "sources": ["L44-L73"]}
],
"risk_indicators": [
{"claim": "The session included print (A0159) and copy (A0386) actions on a record whose active encounter reason is dependent drug abuse; the facts show no standalone concern given the unit and schedule alignment.", "sources": ["L4", "L9", "G24", "G6"]}
],
"missing_information": [
"Whether U0098 was assigned to P01661's care team is not shown in the facts; the disposition rests on unit and schedule alignment, not a confirmed assignment.",
"The destination and handling of the printed (L9) and copied (L4) output is not shown; the officer could confirm secure handling for added assurance."
],
"disposition": "clear",
"priority": "low",
"rationale": "U0098's scheduled MED2 shift (G2) overlaps P01661's MED2 inpatient stay (G6); all accesses occurred during the shift from MED2 workstations (G15, G16), and the user saw many other unit patients (L14-L43). No personal tie exists (G9). Print/copy of a sensitive record (L4, L9, G24) is noted but explained by unit care."
}

{"what_happened": "Pharmacist U0093 accessed the record of P00195, a staff member in the user's own department, on Oct 9 and Oct 11 from PHARM workstations, performing reads and updates. An order for the patient's active inpatient encounter had been sent to the user's department, and the Oct 11 session ran past the scheduled shift end.",
"purpose_evidence": [
{"claim": "An order for encounter E001257 was sent to the user's department PHARM, and that encounter (inpatient MED2, 2026-10-08 to 2026-10-18) was active on both access dates, indicating a pharmacy work reason for the access.", "sources": ["G10", "G5", "L1", "L9"]},
{"claim": "U0093 is a pharmacist in PHARM and made the accesses from PHARM workstations D0201 and D0291.", "sources": ["G1", "G13", "G15", "L1", "L7", "L9"]},
{"claim": "The Oct 9 accesses (11:41-12:15) fell within the scheduled 07:00-15:00 PHARM shift.", "sources": ["G2", "L1", "L6"]},
{"claim": "The user handled many other patients in the same window, consistent with routine pharmacy workload rather than focus on one record.", "sources": ["L10", "L39"]}
